      "writtenOn": "2017-06-03T02:44:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know that the \"mLock\" is traditional, but recently I\u0027ve been pointed to just using synchronized(this) which means that we can just make the methods synchronized in most cases. Especially given the number of them, would that be cleaner than putting all the contents of each method into a synchronized (mLock) block?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 667,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 667,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "7c882e16abcefa77a93480e032b727323571d484",
